# Title: Potentially Suspicious Child Process Of VsCode
# ID: 5a3164f2-b373-4152-93cf-090b13c12d27
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2023-01-26
# Tags: attack.execution, attack.stealth, attack.t1218, attack.t1202
# Description: Detects uncommon or suspicious child processes spawning from a VsCode "code.exe" process. This could indicate an attempt of persistence via VsCode tasks or terminal profiles.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

((parent_name:*\\code.exe) AND (((process_name:*\\powershell.exe OR process_name:*\\pwsh.exe OR process_name:*\\cmd.exe) AND (cmdline:*Invoke-Expressions* OR cmdline:*IEX* OR cmdline:*Invoke-Command* OR cmdline:*ICM* OR cmdline:*DownloadString* OR cmdline:*rundll32* OR cmdline:*regsvr32* OR cmdline:*wscript* OR cmdline:*cscript*)) OR ((process_name:*\\calc.exe OR process_name:*\\regsvr32.exe OR process_name:*\\rundll32.exe OR process_name:*\\cscript.exe OR process_name:*\\wscript.exe)) OR ((process_name:*:\\Users\\Public\\* OR process_name:*:\\Windows\\Temp\\* OR process_name:*:\\Temp\\*))))
